<title>GERMANY: POLL - Economists see contraction in German Q4 GDP.</title>
<headline>POLL - Economists see contraction in German Q4 GDP.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters on Monday and Tuesday gave the following forecasts for expectations for fourth quarter German gross domestic product figures which will be released on Wednesday.</p>
<p>All forecasts, which give the percentage change expected, relate to seasonally adjusted data -</p>
<p>					   Change vs Q3   Change vs Q4 96</p>
<p> Werner Verbockett, Commerzbank	 -0.1	    +1.8</p>
<p> Klaus Baader, DMG, London		-0.3	    +1.7</p>
<p> Mathias Haffner, BZW		     -0.2	    +1.6</p>
<p> Klaus Friedrich, Dresdner Bank	 +0.1	    +1.9</p>
<p> Ulrike Kastens, TCM			-0.2	    +1.6</p>
<p> Thomas Kull, WestLB			+0.2	    +2.0</p>
<p> Armin Kayser, SBC Warburg		-0.2	    +1.6</p>
<p> Ralf Kugelstadt, UBS		     -0.2	    +1.3</p>
<p> Gerhard Lyons, DKB International     -0.2	    +1.6</p>
<p> Hugh Roberts, Nat West Markets	  0.0	    +1.6</p>
<p> Dr. Gerhard Grebe, Bank Julius Br   -0.2	    +1.6</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
